# hsops environment variables (optional)
#
# hsops has no secrets and needs no configuration to run. These two variables
# override where the hooks keep their files. The hooks read them from the process
# environment (for example, export them in your shell profile); they do not load
# a .env file. Leave them unset to use the defaults.

# Data folder for user.md, general lessons and server profiles.
# Read by hooks/_hook.py (data_dir). Default: ~/.config/hsops
# HSOPS_DATA_DIR=/path/to/your/hsops-data

# Folder for per-session hook state (the guard's identical-retry bookkeeping).
# Read by hooks/_hook.py (State). Claude Code normally sets this itself.
# Default: the system temp directory, under hsops-hooks/
# CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA=/path/to/hook-state
